                            <msPart xml:id="p6">
                                <msIdentifier/>
                                <msContents>
                                    <summary>Painting of the '<ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1031VirginAndChild">Virgin Mary</ref>'</summary>
                                    <msItem xml:id="p6_i1">
                                        <locus target="#6v"/>
                                        <title>Description of the painting 'Virgin Mary'</title>
                                        <note>The text following the picture contains the title of the seventh miracle of the Virgin Mary (possibly, according 
                                            the counting of E. A. Budge: <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3593Miracle">Miracle of Mary: Miracle of the young girl called Mary, from
        Dafrā</ref>). The owner, 
                                            <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15036ZamanfasQ">Zamanfas Qeddus</persName> is mentioned as well: 
                                            <foreign xml:lang="gez">፯፡ ተአምሪሃ፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በክልኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ወላዲተ፡ አምላክ። ጸሎታ፡ ወበረከታ፡ ወምሕረተ፡ ፍቁር፡
                                            ወልዳ፡ የሀሉ፡ ምስለ፡ ገብራ፡ ዘመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ለዓለ<sic>ም</sic>፡ ዓለም።</foreign>. It is not clear, whether this text was indeed
                                            included in the description on the verso page of the painting, as it is assumed here, or is possibly copied as a caption 
                                            for the painting on the front page (cf. <ref target="#d6"/>).</note>
                                    </msItem>
                                </msContents>
                                <physDesc>
                                    <objectDesc form="Leaf">
                                        <supportDesc>
                                            <support>
                                                <material key="paper"/>
                                            </support>
                                            <extent>
                                                <measure unit="leaf" quantity="1">1</measure>
                                                <dimensions type="inner" unit="mm">
                                                    <height>430</height>
                                                    <width>350</width>
                                                </dimensions><dimensions subtype="computed" unit="mm" type="inner"><height quantity="430" unit="mm"/><width quantity="350" unit="mm"/></dimensions>
                                            </extent>
                                            <foliation>Numbered '6' on the verso.</foliation>
                                            <condition key="intact"/>        
                                        </supportDesc>
                                    </objectDesc>
                                    <decoDesc>
                                        <decoNote xml:id="d6" type="miniature">
                                            <locus target="#6r"/>
                                            <desc>Tracing of the whole page from manuscript 'Miracles of Mary' (possibly from the 17th century) from the 
                                                'Cathedral Collection of MSS. Axum' (probably <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0344AksumS">ʾAksum Ṣǝyon</placeName>). Found by 
                                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15033Playne">Beatrice Playne</persName> and painted while on the spot. The picture depicts the 
                                                <ref type="authFile" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/AT1031VirginAndChild">Virgin with the Child</ref>, surrounded by six 
                                                women and two men, one of whom carries a sword. The text following the picture contains the title of the seventh 
                                                miracle of Mary (possibly, according the counting of E. A. Budge: <ref type="work" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3593Miracle">Miracle of Mary: Miracle of the young girl called Mary, from
        Dafrā</ref>)
                                                and mentions the owner, <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15036ZamanfasQ">Zamanfas Qǝddus</persName>: <foreign xml:lang="gez">፯፡ ተአምሪሃ፡ 
                                                ለእግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በክልኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ወላዲተ፡ አምላክ። ጸሎታ፡ ወበረከታ፡ ወምሕረተ፡ ፍቁር፡ ወልዳ፡ የሀሉ፡ ምስለ፡ ገብራ፡ ዘመንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡
                                                ለዓለ<sic>ም</sic>፡ ዓለም።</foreign>. It is unclear whether this text was copied as a caption for the painting on 
                                                <locus target="#6r"/> or was included in the description on the back of the painting.</desc>
                                        </decoNote>
                                    </decoDesc>
                                </physDesc>
